    {
      "name": "an alias may declare its OWN container — UCP's two carriers are different SHAPES",
      "$comment": "v1.37 §C.3: the canonical capability is an object-path at extensions.<reverse-domain>.legal-context while the discovery carrier is a tagged-array at links[type=terms_of_service].url. Without a per-alias container one manifest cannot declare both, and the write flag — built for exactly this advice — would be unusable by the one protocol that asks for it.",
      "input": {
        "protocol": "ucp",
        "pattern": "http-advisory",
        "tier": "A",
        "encoding": "reference-object",
        "container": {
          "kind": "object-path"
        },
        "field": "extensions.com-integraledger-legal-context",
        "readAlso": [
