    {
      "name": "an object-path container may declare SEGMENTS — a key containing literal dots is addressable",
      "$comment": "Forced by UCP, whose capability keys follow [reverse-domain].{service}.{capability} — com.integraledger.legal-context is ONE key under `extensions`, not four nested objects. A dot-split locator cannot address it, and hyphenating our capability name to suit the walker would put a spelling on the wire UCP's own naming convention does not use. When segments is present, `field` stays the human-readable locator and segments carries the machine-readable form — the same division of labour tagged-array already established.",
      "input": {
        "protocol": "ucp",
        "pattern": "http-advisory",
        "tier": "A",
        "encoding": "reference-object",
        "container": {
          "kind": "object-path",
          "segments": ["extensions", "com.integraledger.legal-context"]
        },
        "field": "extensions[\"com.integraledger.legal-context\"]",
        "carrierTypes": ["sha256"]
      },
      "expected": true
    },
    {
